  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "SERnOkW/O0CKSE62gZrlKTiuRFk=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:36:09.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Vetra supports collaborative development through remote drives:\n\n- **Without `--remote-drive`**: `ph vetra` boots a local Vetra Switchboard and creates the drive there (solo development)\n- **With `--remote-drive <url>`**: Connects to a shared remote drive, skipping local switchboard initialization\n\nKey workflows:\n- **Project Owner**: `ph init --remote-drive <url>` -> Create GitHub repo -> Push -> `ph vetra --watch`\n- **Collaborator**: `git clone <repo>` -> `pnpm install` -> `ph vetra --watch`\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f **The collaborator step used to be `ph checkout --remote-drive <url>`, and that command no longer exists as far as the CLI is concerned.** It survives only as `clis/ph-cmd/legacy/commands/checkout.ts`, registered in neither `phCliCommandNames` (`packages/shared/clis/command-names.ts`) nor the `ph` entrypoint's cmd-ts subcommand tree (`clis/ph-cmd/src/commands/ph.ts` \u2192 `init`, `use`, `update`, `setup-globals`, `use-local` + help commands). The `legacy/` directory is excluded from tsconfig and never built or published; the file would not even compile, since it imports a `../utils/package-manager.js` that does not exist. The academy still teaches it in five places across two pages, and `COMMANDS-LEGACY.md` documents it as well \u2014 all stale. There is no replacement command: `ph init --remote-drive` is for *creating* a project bound to a drive, so joining an existing one is the manual clone-and-install shown above.\n\nThe clone works as a substitute for one specific reason: the repo's committed `powerhouse.config.json` already carries the `vetra` block, and `ph vetra`'s `--remote-drive` option has a `defaultValue` that reads `getConfig().vetra?.driveUrl`. So a fresh clone picks up the team's drive with no flags. If the block is missing, hand-edit it in or pass `ph vetra --remote-drive <url>` every time \u2014 nothing in the CLI can write that key after `ph init` (its only two writers are codegen scaffold paths, and `getConfig` is read-only). Note also that only `driveUrl` is ever read back; `driveId` is written and then ignored.\n\nBe aware of a live trap on the owner's side too: if you point `ph init --remote-drive` at a drive that has already been configured with a GitHub URL, `clis/ph-cli/src/utils/validate-remote-drive.ts` prints an error telling you to \"use the checkout command instead\" \u2014 the dead command \u2014 and because `clis/ph-cli/src/services/init.ts` ignores that validation failure, it then reports success and scaffolds a new project regardless.\n\nThe **preview drive** (created with `--watch` / `-w` mode) provides a safe testing environment:\n- The main \"Vetra\" drive syncs with the remote and contains stable configuration\n- The \"Vetra Preview\" drive is local-only for testing document models and editors before syncing\n\nRemote drive configuration is stored in `powerhouse.config.json`:\n```json\n\"vetra\": {\n  \"driveId\": \"bai-specifications\",\n  \"driveUrl\": \"https://switchboard.staging.vetra.io/d/bai-specifications\"\n}\n```\n\nIts type is `vetra?: { driveId: string; driveUrl: string }` (`packages/shared/clis/types.ts`), and the JSON schema marks both fields required with `additionalProperties: false`.\n\n_Source-verified 2026-08-13 against Powerhouse source at v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:36:09.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:36:09.000Z"
    }
  },
